{"id": "clm:19a4db6fbd9074990da07b582305fb714e6f45591c4dd4e599f17aaf4cd8b6a0", "type": "statement", "text": "For Atlas infrastructure, a defensible design is one environment root and state boundary per application/environment project, reusing modules. This is a synthesis: MongoDB recommends separate production projects per application/environment, while Google documents environment roots with shared modules. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/architecture/current/hierarchy.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Multi-Environment Terraform Directories vs Workspaces"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "definition", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://docs.cloud.google.com/docs/terraform/best-practices/root-modules?hl=en"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:7ba41ee0e049fbc975660e4f6a29ba0c873f1c8c0a99edc6b0cad4a09ebf610b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:06cbdb7c7e534fc20f27a825bdc626d517980417ef463c3cf3a8175a46a6260b", "ev:6100b03de04dcf5714c5064648d259cf74a0f97f16413e8d5d3134d59d314098"]}
{"id": "clm:71d8f86326ce705551cb7f9aa7a0ec86d692146f6c524ea71651c9e13bbbeb69", "type": "statement", "text": "Environment directories have maintenance costs. Terragrunt reduces repeated backend configuration through inherited settings and generated backend files, but adds another tool and configuration layer; its directory approach still requires more environment files than CLI workspaces. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.gruntwork.io/blog/how-to-manage-multiple-environments-with-terraform-using-terragrunt", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Multi-Environment Terraform Directories vs Workspaces"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "structure", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:7ba41ee0e049fbc975660e4f6a29ba0c873f1c8c0a99edc6b0cad4a09ebf610b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:06a641894bbd289bb1e7fadd088724c53d7ca97936331e7ba7ab016ddf33948e", "ev:20681653ce4836cefca6d9bc6eca833ddcf8e7eb8dc7ee34975db8abdb1d928f"]}
{"id": "clm:b13e0344b6032529037ae51bb2bc50c74c6629de6ed95a37b4e2bc1aef17a42f", "type": "statement", "text": "MongoDB recommends separate Atlas projects for application/environment pairs, particularly in production, because project-level settings and permissions define important isolation boundaries. Applying that guidance to Terraform suggests mapping separately controlled deployments to the relevant Atlas projects; directory names or CLI workspace names alone do not enforce those Atlas boundaries. The mapping is an architectural inference, not a MongoDB-mandated repository layout. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/architecture/current/hierarchy.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Multi-Environment Terraform Directories vs Workspaces"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/cloud-docs/workspaces"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:7ba41ee0e049fbc975660e4f6a29ba0c873f1c8c0a99edc6b0cad4a09ebf610b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:06cbdb7c7e534fc20f27a825bdc626d517980417ef463c3cf3a8175a46a6260b", "ev:72ebf018265ea6d8c57b4fc67c858360f16a2f0c2edaa948fffce75d547b86f6"]}
{"id": "clm:66e2881b0b0902f8fa4fc4f73ae0ad8ab66a34f565bb43046fa9e92906833a89", "type": "statement", "text": "Avoid treating workspace switches as system decomposition: components requiring separate configurations and backends should be separated explicitly. Google additionally warns that extensive terraform.workspace conditionals can make configuration harder to read. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/cli/workspaces", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Multi-Environment Terraform Directories vs Workspaces"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "how-to", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://docs.cloud.google.com/docs/terraform/best-practices/root-modules?hl=en"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:7ba41ee0e049fbc975660e4f6a29ba0c873f1c8c0a99edc6b0cad4a09ebf610b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:6100b03de04dcf5714c5064648d259cf74a0f97f16413e8d5d3134d59d314098", "ev:db61cbe2b74f11de09dae7acb2bb80692879a3f8467dd9cbcadf76358fc9d68d"]}
{"id": "clm:92cadee86e8b0e2a87b989a1ea751faf3a4e2a6e52579c3280d9ff30d412502e", "type": "statement", "text": "A Terraform 1.3.9 issue reported that setting TF_WORKSPACE without a cloud workspace mapping still produced \"Missing workspace mapping strategy\". Treat this as a historical integration report, not proof of a current defect or general CLI workspace failure. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://github.com/hashicorp/terraform/issues/33636", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Multi-Environment Terraform Directories vs Workspaces"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:7ba41ee0e049fbc975660e4f6a29ba0c873f1c8c0a99edc6b0cad4a09ebf610b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:f8c2a6c2947aeb8e636e57b713ae47f434268b66cae785f7202250f7fc87a2d3"]}
{"id": "clm:706c6e797538cbe9338e25329866baf148c7f730ab2bbb71843ae6fe2f9c0ab1", "type": "statement", "text": "HCP Terraform workspaces differ from CLI workspaces: they contain configuration, variables, and state and can have individual access controls. HashiCorp recommends one HCP workspace per infrastructure component per environment. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/cli/workspaces", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Multi-Environment Terraform Directories vs Workspaces"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/cloud-docs/recommended-practices/part1"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:7ba41ee0e049fbc975660e4f6a29ba0c873f1c8c0a99edc6b0cad4a09ebf610b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:56e15c0a072a9eb133c66da633f667a742dc8887ecb7ddeab02a28fd8e6fa6bb", "ev:60e8461721706bb3ce41cb0679c0001d07b9d29027550647bbf0bbcf5e970d7d"]}
{"id": "clm:a9682d0470a5323203efc9df973dff9b1289f2100e30d7a5d700d08b7c99b12e", "type": "statement", "text": "HCP Terraform workspaces differ from CLI workspaces: each has its own configuration, variables, state and run history, and workspace permissions can delegate access to teams. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/cli/workspaces", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Multi-Environment Terraform Directories vs Workspaces"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/cloud-docs/workspaces"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:7ba41ee0e049fbc975660e4f6a29ba0c873f1c8c0a99edc6b0cad4a09ebf610b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:60e8461721706bb3ce41cb0679c0001d07b9d29027550647bbf0bbcf5e970d7d", "ev:9960965b66bb9194a06e900160a275e5ae656e48e2e1b15be7c746ed6096ee13"]}
{"id": "clm:4db5e3c282c26e32842ccf249ecfae5fdbc7df8ca6f2da8e78ade317371511b8", "type": "statement", "text": "A directory-per-environment pattern can keep root configurations small: declare each environment's backend and instantiate shared modules with environment-specific inputs instead of duplicating resource definitions. Google Cloud explicitly recommends this layout and using only the default CLI workspace in each environment directory. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://docs.cloud.google.com/docs/terraform/best-practices/root-modules?hl=en", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Multi-Environment Terraform Directories vs Workspaces"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.gruntwork.io/blog/how-to-manage-multiple-environments-with-terraform-using-terragrunt"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:7ba41ee0e049fbc975660e4f6a29ba0c873f1c8c0a99edc6b0cad4a09ebf610b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:6100b03de04dcf5714c5064648d259cf74a0f97f16413e8d5d3134d59d314098"]}
{"id": "clm:975d6387bfa94d7a91a4fa1850fe425006fda7404afccd8984c3f9e7687e5de7", "type": "statement", "text": "CLI workspaces remain useful for temporary feature-branch environments using the same configuration and backend. They reuse a working copy and plugin/module caches, reducing overhead compared with maintaining separate working directories. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/cli/workspaces", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Multi-Environment Terraform Directories vs Workspaces"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:7ba41ee0e049fbc975660e4f6a29ba0c873f1c8c0a99edc6b0cad4a09ebf610b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:bbfc983fb7917120c2d740826c6eb9fc898d337603830effb54fd1905b22c5aa"]}
{"id": "clm:d960e08da329f6060cc6a99cc49c651e3fc631cf0a1e03ad01c00c62d71415c6", "type": "statement", "text": "Terraform CLI workspaces keep separate state instances within one working directory while reusing its configuration and backend; selecting a workspace changes which state most Terraform commands operate on. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/cli/workspaces", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Multi-Environment Terraform Directories vs Workspaces"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.gruntwork.io/blog/how-to-manage-terraform-state"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:7ba41ee0e049fbc975660e4f6a29ba0c873f1c8c0a99edc6b0cad4a09ebf610b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:af46b71430c69d4a675ac4cca5de76f2ac7fd5c7720629c9f7c3a1e11d916456"]}
{"id": "clm:caeabe7349232dba393fcf95ecda46985d3e50f3c661b27826a262d41b32c90f", "type": "statement", "text": "For production environments requiring separate credentials and access controls, use separate root configurations and backend access boundaries. Separate folders alone do not enforce permission isolation. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/cli/workspaces", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Multi-Environment Terraform Directories vs Workspaces"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://docs.cloud.google.com/docs/terraform/best-practices/root-modules?hl=en", "https://www.gruntwork.io/blog/how-to-manage-terraform-state"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:7ba41ee0e049fbc975660e4f6a29ba0c873f1c8c0a99edc6b0cad4a09ebf610b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:6100b03de04dcf5714c5064648d259cf74a0f97f16413e8d5d3134d59d314098", "ev:db61cbe2b74f11de09dae7acb2bb80692879a3f8467dd9cbcadf76358fc9d68d"]}
{"id": "clm:d7f0588b08a013d6df3181dd72611c027b605569c4a8c9e95ac688970ef175cc", "type": "statement", "text": "Environment directories can avoid wholesale configuration duplication: place reusable infrastructure in child modules and instantiate them from dev, qa, and prod roots, each declaring its own backend location and inputs. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://docs.cloud.google.com/docs/terraform/best-practices/root-modules?hl=en", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Multi-Environment Terraform Directories vs Workspaces"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/cli/workspaces"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:7ba41ee0e049fbc975660e4f6a29ba0c873f1c8c0a99edc6b0cad4a09ebf610b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:6100b03de04dcf5714c5064648d259cf74a0f97f16413e8d5d3134d59d314098", "ev:db61cbe2b74f11de09dae7acb2bb80692879a3f8467dd9cbcadf76358fc9d68d"]}
{"id": "clm:24bfd90c845e3d45887da28f43df370f27cb218dfd94e335b4a158a745c569c5", "type": "statement", "text": "CLI workspaces remain useful for temporary parallel copies and tests of substantially identical infrastructure. Rejecting every use of workspaces overstates the isolation guidance. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/cli/workspaces", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Multi-Environment Terraform Directories vs Workspaces"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.gruntwork.io/blog/how-to-manage-terraform-state"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:7ba41ee0e049fbc975660e4f6a29ba0c873f1c8c0a99edc6b0cad4a09ebf610b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:bbfc983fb7917120c2d740826c6eb9fc898d337603830effb54fd1905b22c5aa"]}
{"id": "clm:012fe47dd73b647a0edbeb7ef593822f921b505a8ee22d6137fe22733446ff27", "type": "statement", "text": "Terraform CLI workspaces separate state within one working directory and backend; they do not by themselves provide different backend credentials or access-control boundaries between environments. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://developer.hashicorp.com/terraform/cli/workspaces", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Multi-Environment Terraform Directories vs Workspaces"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://docs.cloud.google.com/docs/terraform/best-practices/root-modules?hl=en"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:7ba41ee0e049fbc975660e4f6a29ba0c873f1c8c0a99edc6b0cad4a09ebf610b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:db61cbe2b74f11de09dae7acb2bb80692879a3f8467dd9cbcadf76358fc9d68d"]}
{"id": "clm:85b9769ff64ba1985696e4d50327fc351237c2a1ab68955a620644c5496ae282", "type": "statement", "text": "Directory-based deployments can pin different module releases in development, staging and production, allowing promotion after testing. Gruntwork demonstrates this with separate Terragrunt configurations using Git source refs; changing a shared local module path alone does not provide independent version pinning. (low confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.gruntwork.io/blog/how-to-manage-multiple-environments-with-terraform-using-terragrunt", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Multi-Environment Terraform Directories vs Workspaces"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:7ba41ee0e049fbc975660e4f6a29ba0c873f1c8c0a99edc6b0cad4a09ebf610b", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:f8330c8d8bcc47343f094ded5bd09117af6284e906ad827c0acd19043310c7a5"]}
